{#- A page built from blocks, for the browser editor Pages CMS (Output Claude/77_Keuze webeditor voor Raphael.html).
    The page's front matter has "blocks": a list, each with a "type" that names a file in page-blocks/. Editors can add,
    move and remove blocks; the look of each block stays in its file, in the site's house style.
    Each block writes its own HTML. Its texts are Markdown and go through the "markdown" filters (eleventy.config.js),
    the same Markdown library as the text of a page, so the page looks exactly as it did when it was written as text.
    A block with "hidden: true" is kept but not shown. Block texts are never run as Nunjucks code. -#}
{%- for b in blocks %}{% if b.type and not b.hidden %}{% include "page-blocks/" + b.type + ".njk" %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
